From 4701782b0d47b6109927401dbd4e2ae2b22f71e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 08:27:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: restructure the dealer sidebar into collapsible
 groups (item 16)

16 flat links (grown from the original set as ID Cards, Business
Documents, and Marketing Materials were added this session) into 5
short, labeled, collapsible groups: Inventory & Sales, Team, Design
Studio, Operations, Account - plus Overview as its own standalone
link at the top, always visible.

Only the group containing whatever page you're currently on starts
expanded; the rest start collapsed. This is the actual fix for 'too
large' - the visible height drops from 16 items to effectively 5
group headers plus whichever few are relevant to where you are, while
every single link stays fully reachable - nothing was removed, only
organized.

Real UX bug caught and fixed before committing: my first version had
the expand/collapse chevron rotation backwards - pointing down when
collapsed and up when expanded, the opposite of the standard,
intuitive pattern (closed = pointing right/down toward more content,
open = pointing down/toward the now-visible content). Fixed to
collapsed = pointing right, expanded = rotated down.

Verified programmatically that all 15 grouped links plus the
standalone Overview link account for exactly the same 16 destinations
that existed before - none dropped in the restructure.
